05","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229777,"global_rank":113339,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19624},{"name":"prismofeverything/organism-legacy","owner":"prismofeverything","html_url":"https://github.com/prismofeverything/organism-legacy","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":8,"language":"Python","description":"implementation of the organism board game","topics":[],"score":229758,"global_rank":113354,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19625},{"name":"kevinslin/dotfiles","owner":"kevinslin","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinslin/dotfiles","stars":3,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Some helpful dotfiles","topics":[],"score":229740,"global_rank":113365,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19626},{"name":"sushiroll-206/Tanuki","owner":"sushiroll-206","html_url":"https://github.com/sushiroll-206/Tanuki","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Tanuki is a NLP powered Resume matcher that aims to increase the chance for  job seekers to land an interview. ","topics":[],"score":229737,"global_rank":113376,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19627},{"name":"rbavery/satlas-aoti","owner":"rbavery","html_url":"